-- AlterEnum
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff` against a throwaway database carrying every
-- prior migration, not hand-written. `migrate dev` could not be used: this
-- branch's schema.prisma and its migrations already disagree about several
-- Timesheet constraint names and seven unique constraints, so `migrate dev`
-- refuses to proceed without a reset. That drift predates this change and is
-- recorded separately; only the enum value below belongs to it.
--
-- Additive and safe. PostgreSQL will not allow a new enum value to be *used* in
-- the same transaction that adds it, which is why this migration only adds it —
-- the first write of NOT_DELIVERED happens at runtime, long after.
ALTER TYPE "EmailDeliveryStatus" ADD VALUE 'NOT_DELIVERED';
